.Dd September 24, 2026
.Dt NETUP 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm netup
.Nd bring up interfaces from the network configuration file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl a
.Op Ar interface ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads
.Pa /etc/network/interfaces
in the
.Ic ifup
format and configures the selected interfaces.
With no operands or with
.Fl a ,
it includes every interface named by an
.Ic auto
or
.Ic allow-hotplug
line.
An interface named on the command line needs neither declaration.
The file is read in two passes through one open stream.
A read or seek error aborts configuration before any interface is changed.
.Pp
The supported declarations are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic auto Ar name
Include the interface when no operands or
.Fl a
are given.
.It Ic allow-hotplug Ar name
Include the interface in the same way as
.Ic auto .
.It Ic iface Ar name Ic inet dhcp
Run
.Xr dhcpc 8
for the interface.
The client stays in the foreground until its first discovery round
has completed.
.It Ic iface Ar name Ic inet static
Apply a static configuration.
The stanza requires
.Ic address
and
.Ic netmask
entries; a
.Ic gateway
entry is optional.
.El
.Pp
A static stanza is validated in full before any
.Xr ioctl 2
changes the interface.
Static configuration fails if the DHCP client's PID file identifies a
running process, contains no valid positive process ID, or cannot be read.
.Pp
On a boot with
.Ql rach2.ip=none ,
init-metal performs the same configuration job.
On os-real, BusyBox's
.Ic ifup
performs this job.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/network/interfaces
.It Pa /etc/network/interfaces
Interface declarations and DHCP or static stanzas.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl netup -a
The
.Ql tests/run netif
suite exercises DHCP and static stanzas.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
An unknown option produces
.Ql "usage: netup [-a] [interface ...]" .
A DHCP client that stops before it reaches the background produces
.Ql "netup: INTERFACE: dhcpc exited with status N before reaching the background"
or
.Ql "netup: INTERFACE: dhcpc was killed by signal N before reaching the background" ;
such a client may have left its address on the interface.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr busybox-networking 1 ,
.Xr recovery 7 ,
.Xr dhcpc 8
